ID: B3-Ch09b-Backup
TEXT:

"Alright," I say. "Let's go to the Overseer first, then. Can you teleport us there now?"

"I'm on it!" Flower says. White light flares around us, blinding and absolute.

"Here we are!"

The glare clears into the boundless radiance of the ether. Hovering right beside us, the Overseer's green-eyed drone hums in place.

"Processing. Processing..." the drone's voice carries cleanly through the glow. "The Overseer protocol now understands why it could not locate your party anywhere within the ether. Having witnessed your teleportation capability, the working assumption is that you relocated to an undetectable sanctuary. Is that assessment accurate?"

"Um, yeah," Flower says. "That's right. Wait—you were looking for us?"

"Affirmative," the Overseer says. "The Overseer protocol apologizes for the inconvenience. Your souls were not intended for ejection alongside the rebel forces. The displacement routine remains experimental and encompassed the entire perimeter instead of isolating our designated targets."

"Oh, it's fine!" Flower says. "Everyone's in one piece. We actually came to ask if you want to team up against Peter and the king of the underground out here on the ethereal plane. I can jump us straight to them."

"The Overseer protocol accepts your proposal," the drone responds. "That was my projected vector as well."

"Great!" Flower says. "Brace yourselves. Jumping in three... two... one..."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch09b-Challenge, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Challenge)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Challenge
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0) {
"The Overseer doesn't have his drone swarm out here, so I doubt he'll be much help," I tell Flower. "Let's take Peter on ourselves."

"If you say so, Barry," Flower says. "Hold on. I'm jumping us in."

"Ready," I say. The familiar white flash envelops us, humming through every nerve before tearing away.

"What are you doing here?" Peter's voice cuts through the stillness the moment the jump resolves.

Twenty feet ahead in the vast white expanse, Peter stands beside the king of the underground, who has already shaped a physical body out of ethereal matter. Peter's eyes are dull and dark, without a flicker of the incandescent blaze pouring from Flower's face; the evolutionary shift that gave her long-range soul tracking and instantaneous transit never touched him.

"Take a wild guess," I say.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 1) {
"What are you doing here?" Peter's voice cuts through the stillness the moment the jump resolves.

Twenty feet ahead in the vast white expanse, Peter stands beside the king of the underground, who has already shaped a physical body out of ethereal matter. Peter's eyes are dull and dark, without a flicker of the incandescent blaze pouring from Flower's face; the evolutionary shift that gave her long-range soul tracking and instantaneous transit never touched him.

"Take a wild guess," I say.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_conclusions != 1) {
"This is a mistake," Peter says, hands low and steady. "You have no business challenging me here. Turn back while you still have the chance."

"Sorry," I say. "Not happening."

"You don't understand what you're stepping into," Peter says. "The Overseer is my only target in this realm. Walk away, and we can still—"

"Peter, forgive the interruption," the king says, raising a hand. "A brief question before we engage."

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0 && v_b3_ch9_conclusions == 1) {
"Under ordinary circumstances, I would assume you came seeking an alliance against the Overseer," the king says, his gaze weighing me down. "Yet from your tone, that holds no truth. Am I to understand that every promise you made before the breach was hollow, and you chose betrayal after all?"

"Pretty much," I say.

"This is a mistake," Peter says, hands low and steady. "You have no business challenging me here. Turn back while you still have the chance."

"Sorry," I say. "Not happening."

"You don't understand what you're stepping into," Peter says. "The Overseer is my only target in this realm. Walk away, and we can still—"

"Peter, forgive the interruption," the king says, raising a hand. "A brief question before we engage."

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 1 && v_b3_ch9_conclusions == 1) {
"Under ordinary circumstances, I would assume you came seeking an alliance against the Overseer," the king says, his gaze fixed on the machine beside us. "Yet seeing you arrive in lockstep with the enemy leaves little room for doubt. Am I to understand that every promise you made before the breach was hollow, and you chose betrayal after all?"

"Pretty much," I say.

"This is a mistake," Peter says, hands low and steady. "You have no business challenging me here. Turn back while you still have the chance."

"Sorry," I say. "Not happening."

"You don't understand what you're stepping into," Peter says. "The Overseer is my only target in this realm. Walk away, and we can still—"

"Peter, forgive the interruption," the king says, raising a hand. "A brief question before we engage."

}
