ID: B3-Ch09b-Logical
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0) {
"Yes, my king?" Peter asks.

"You explained that my earthen form anchors itself to my soul on this plane through its aura, correct?"

"Yes, sir," Peter says.

"Then if that aura binds to my soul," the king continues, "it follows that the soul itself carries an innate aura to receive the link."

"I... had not considered it in those terms," Peter admits, "but in principle, yes. That holds."

"Good!" The king smiles faintly. "Then the sensation is real."

He thrusts an open palm forward. An invisible shockwave slams through the air, shoving me and Flower ten feet backward across the glow.

"Weaker than in the flesh, but workable," the king says, rolling his shoulders as he faces us. "Pardon the delay. I am ready when you are. Give the signal, and we begin."

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 1) {
"Yes, my king?" Peter asks.

"You explained that my earthen form anchors itself to my soul on this plane through its aura, correct?"

"Yes, sir," Peter says.

"Then if that aura binds to my soul," the king continues, "it follows that the soul itself carries an innate aura to receive the link."

"I... had not considered it in those terms," Peter admits, "but in principle, yes. That holds."

"Good!" The king smiles faintly. "Then the sensation is real."

He thrusts an open palm forward. An invisible shockwave slams through the air, shoving me, Flower, and the Overseer ten feet backward across the glow.

"Weaker than in the flesh, but workable," the king says, rolling his shoulders as he faces us. "Pardon the delay. I am ready when you are. Give the signal, and we begin."

}
"Fine by me," I say, dropping into a low stance and snapping through the hand forms, drawing mana to my fingertips. "Signal given."

Before the king can plant his feet, a jagged bolt of lightning rips from my index finger, streaking for his chest. It collides an inch from his tunic, throwing bright blue sparks against a dense, invisible shell of hardened aura without budging him.

Flower follows instantly, hurling a rapid volley of fireballs into their line. The explosions bloom and clear to reveal a thick dome of ice encasing them both, steam hissing off its surface as the outer layer slumps and melts under the heat.

"A formidable opening, little girl," the king says as the ice collapses into vapor. "One could almost mistake that for lethal intent."

choice(""Nobody is trying to kill anyone. All we want is to defeat you and bring this war to an end."", B3-Ch09b-Impenetrable, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Impenetrable, v_b3_ch9_assassinate = 0)
choice(""Of course we're trying to kill you. That's what you get for plotting to assassinate us."", B3-Ch09b-Impenetrable, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Impenetrable, v_b3_ch9_assassinate = 1)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Impenetrable
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch9_assassinate == 0) {
"Nobody is trying to kill anyone. All we want is to defeat you and bring this war to an end."

"Is that so?" The king tilts his head. "Then let us call this a spirited contest between former comrades with divergent ideals. Now... let us see what those newly forged spells of yours can do."

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_assassinate == 1) {
"Of course we're trying to kill you. That's what you get for plotting to assassinate us."

"Still determined to cast me as the monster," the king says quietly. "A pity. I truly hoped we might settle our differences with some semblance of dignity."

"Do you still wish me to show restraint, sire?" Peter asks.

"Only so long as your life is not forfeit," the king replies. "If the balance tips, you have full leave to use everything at your disposal."

He turns back toward me. "Now... let us see what those newly forged spells of yours can do."

}
The king sweeps both arms outward. In a heartbeat, four shimmering, semi-transparent barriers snap into place around Flower and me, forming a sealed cube identical to the barriers Talmak's elven subordinate deployed in the arena. The temperature inside plummets instantly; frost creeps along my sleeves, the chill biting so fiercely that another thirty seconds in here will turn our blood to slush.

"Hold on," Flower says, grabbing my wrist. "Jumping us out."

Light flares, the world vibrating violently around us. When the jump snaps clear, we stand outside the enclosure—only for four fresh semi-transparent walls to lock around us in the same instant. The air inside freezes at terrifying speed as Peter channels another wave of frost through the seal.

choice("Tell Flower to teleport us closer to the king and Peter this time.", B3-Ch09b-Blabbering, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Blabbering, v_b3_ch9_teleport = 0)
choice("Tell Flower that we should move in separate directions as soon as we teleport again.", B3-Ch09b-Separate, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Separate, v_b3_ch9_teleport = 1)
choice("Ask Flower if she can attack the king with a pillar of fire to break his concentration.", B3-Ch09b-Blabbering, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Blabbering, v_b3_ch9_teleport = 2)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Separate
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b3_ch9_assassinate == 0 && v_b3_ch9_backup == 0 || v_b3_ch9_assassinate == 1 && v_b3_ch9_backup == 0)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b3_ch9_backup == 1)
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0) {
"Let's move in opposite directions the second we jump," I whisper to Flower. "He can't hold two distinct enclosures at once with that aura technique."

"Got it," Flower says. "Brace yourself!"

Her fingers dig into my forearm. The light snaps, and we materialize outside the perimeter, instantly breaking away from each other to split his focus.

The gamble fails immediately. Two shimmering barriers drop over us in the same breath, sealing me in one cube and Flower in another. Peter doesn't miss a beat; freezing air rushes through both enclosures, frosting my knuckles within seconds.

Across the gap, Flower lunges into a second jump, flashing directly inside my box to seize my arm. A third flash rips us both into the open air, but the moment she lets go, she stumbles, clutching her temples with a sharp intake of breath.

"Flower, what's wrong?"

"I... pushed the jumps too hard..." she gasps, kneeling on empty air. "Give me a second... my head..."

"You have no seconds left," the king says, his voice flat as four fresh barriers lock into place around us. Frost surges across the floor, racing up our boots. "Unless your companion possesses an improvised teleportation routine ready to deploy in the next fifteen seconds. At this point, little from him would genuinely surprise me."

His voice fades behind a roar of frantic analysis. Every particle diagram, every counter-curse and basic movement formula from twenty years of notebooks blurs past my mind's eye. Nothing fits. The cold sinks past the skin, gnawing into bone until my teeth chatter so violently I can barely hold a thought.

Flower tries to gather mana, but her hands shake apart before the sequence can form. The freeze thickens, dragging our eyelids down. Weight crushes my chest, and the sea of light dims to black.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 1) {
"Let's move in opposite directions the second we jump," I whisper to Flower. "He can't hold two distinct enclosures at once with that aura technique."

"Got it," Flower says. "Brace yourself!"

Her fingers dig into my forearm. The light snaps, and we materialize outside the perimeter, instantly breaking away from each other to split his focus.

The gamble fails immediately. Two shimmering barriers drop over us in the same breath, sealing me in one cube and Flower in another. Peter doesn't miss a beat; freezing air rushes through both enclosures, frosting my knuckles within seconds.

Across the gap, Flower lunges into a second jump, flashing directly inside my box to seize my arm. A third flash rips us both into the open air, but the moment she lets go, she stumbles, clutching her temples with a sharp intake of breath.

"Flower, what's wrong?"

"I... pushed the jumps too hard..." she gasps, kneeling on empty air. "Give me a second... my head..."

"You have no seconds left," the king says, his voice flat as four fresh barriers lock into place around us. Frost surges across the floor, racing up our boots. "Unless your companion possesses an improvised teleportation routine ready to deploy in the next fifteen seconds. At this point, little from him would genuinely surprise me—"

A searing lance of fire crashes into the king's flank.

The barrier around us shatters as the king jerks his focus back, pouring every shred of aura into reinforcing his personal shield against the blazing torrent.

We scramble clear of the freezing zone. Hovering thirty feet out, the Overseer's drone channels a continuous jet of white-hot flame from its chassis.

"Apologies for the delay," the Overseer drones. "I was uncertain whether your confinement was tactical bait or a critical failure."

"It's fine," I say, sucking in ragged breaths. "Keep the pressure on him. Don't let him reset."

"Understood."

With the drone pinning the king and Flower catching her breath, I turn my sights on Peter, snapping my hands through the lightning sequence and unleashing a bolt at his chest.

Peter doesn't dodge. His fingers mirror my exact motions in reverse, fluid and instantaneous. My lightning dissolves into thin air the moment it reaches his outstretched palm.

The Brinhorn dispel. This bastard is throwing my own technique right back in my face.

"What are you muttering about?" Peter demands, his brow furrowing. "'Your own technique'? If that was an attempt at misdirection, choose a more convincing lie."

Damn it. I let the thought slip through without filtering out the words.

I clamp down on my inner voice. The Brinhorn dispel has one fatal flaw: the caster must read the incoming spell fast enough to reverse the geometry and complete the entire counter-sequence before the original spell resolves. That makes multi-step dispelling exceptionally vulnerable to a feint.

Let's hope none of that leaked into the ether.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_assassinate == 0 && v_b3_ch9_backup == 0) {
Voices drift through a heavy fog. Low, tight, edged with tension. I try to force my eyes open, but my limbs refuse to respond; paralysis holds every muscle rigid.

"We cannot leave them behind," the king says. "They will be torn apart out here."

"With respect, sire—why concern yourself with their fate?" Peter's voice is stiff. "They betrayed our movement. They stood with the Overseer. We owe them nothing."

"Their enmity in this hour does not erase the blood they spilled on our behalf," the king replies. "Wake them before we depart. Let them face whatever follows on their own feet."

"As you command, my lord," Peter says. "I will wake the girl only. The man may know the counter to my transit spell, and I will not take that risk."

A high vibrational hum builds and cuts off sharply. Silence settles for several long heartbeats—broken by hands grabbing my tunic, violently shaking me as Flower's screams pierce my ears.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_assassinate == 1 && v_b3_ch9_backup == 0) {
Voices drift through a heavy fog. Low, tight, edged with tension. I try to force my eyes open, but my limbs refuse to respond; paralysis holds every muscle rigid.

"We cannot leave them behind," the king says. "They will be torn apart out here."

"With respect, sire—why concern yourself with their fate?" Peter's voice is stiff. "They came with explicit intent to execute us. We owe them nothing."

"Their enmity in this hour does not erase the blood they spilled on our behalf," the king replies. "Wake them before we depart. Let them face whatever follows on their own feet."

"As you command, my lord," Peter says. "I will wake the girl only. The man may know the counter to my transit spell, and I will not take that risk."

A high vibrational hum builds and cuts off sharply. Silence settles for several long heartbeats—broken by hands grabbing my tunic, violently shaking me as Flower's screams pierce my ears.

}
