ID: B3-Ch09b-Melding
TEXT:

"Barry, wake up!" Flower's voice cracks with panic. "You're fading! Please, Barry, open your eyes!"

I force my eyelids apart. The white glow shines straight through my own forearms; my hands are translucent silhouettes, thinning into vapor. A hollow, sickening wave of vertigo churns through my gut as my awareness slips between the cold rain of Ollendor and the glaring void of the ether.

"Barry, look at me!" Flower grips my shoulders, her red eyes burning wide. "Can you picture the cube? The place where your mind stays? Visualize it!"

Her words float past like sound carried over water. My thoughts drift, disconnected from the hollow outline of my body. A spectator watching the final moments from a great distance. The exhaustion is absolute. Everything pulls toward sleep.

"Barry, please!" Flower's hands press into my chest, flaring with heat that doesn't warm me. "Say something—gods, you're almost gone! Barry, hold on! Barry!!!"

Her shouts fade to a distant whisper. The transparency spreads to my chest; the ache and nausea drain away, replaced by an eerie, weightless quiet. The boundaries of my mind dissolve into the surrounding light, particle by particle, until there is no thought, no memory, no self.

Only the quiet.

