ID: B3-Ch09b-Blabbering
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch9_teleport == 0) {
"Drop us right on top of them," I murmur to Flower. "He won't drop the cube if it boxes him in with us."

"On it," Flower says. "Hang on!"

Light engulfs us. We rematerialize five feet from the king and Peter. Caught off guard by the proximity, the king foregoes the enclosure, thrusting an open palm forward to blow us back with an aura blast.

Flower beats him to the draw. A blazing column of fire erupts from her hands, forcing the king to wrench his power into a solid barrier against the inferno. With his attention locked on the flames, I snap my fingers through the lightning sequence and loose a bolt at Peter.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_teleport == 2) {
"Hit the king with a pillar of fire from below," I tell Flower. "Crack his focus."

"Trying now!"

A geyser of flame roars upward beneath the king's boots. The sudden heat forces him to release the box, redirecting every shred of aura into a curved shield to deflect the blaze. With his concentration broken, I snap through the hand motions and fire the lightning bolt straight at Peter.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_teleport == 0 || v_b3_ch9_teleport == 2) {
Peter doesn't dodge. His hands mirror my exact motions in reverse, fluid and instantaneous. My lightning dissolves into thin air the moment it reaches his outstretched palm.

The Brinhorn dispel. This bastard is throwing my own technique right back in my face.

"What are you muttering about?" Peter demands, his brow furrowing. "'Your own technique'? If that was an attempt at misdirection, choose a more convincing lie."

Damn it. I let the thought slip through without filtering out the words.

I clamp down on my inner voice. The Brinhorn dispel has one fatal flaw: the caster must read the incoming spell fast enough to reverse the geometry and complete the entire counter-sequence before the original spell resolves. That makes multi-step dispelling exceptionally vulnerable to a feint.

Let's hope none of that leaked into the ether.

}
