ID: B3-Ch09b-Illusory
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch9_listen == 0) {
I ignore the voice's warning, snapping my fingers through the lightning sequence while Peter stares into the white void. The bolt catches him dead-center before his hands can rise into a reverse dispel. The arc snaps through his chest, lifting him off his feet.

"You... treacherous... miserable..."

Peter's eyes roll back, his form slumping into the ether as the illusory manticores dissolve into mist.

I bank hard toward the king, falling into formation beside Flower.

"Flower, on three!" I shout. "Combined focus!"

"Wait—what about the voice?" Flower yells over the roar of her flames. "It said to leave!"

"I didn't stare down the Magium twice to get chased off by ethereal mood swings," I say. "If the ether waited this long, it can wait sixty more seconds. The king is the last piece on the board. We end this now."

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_listen == 1) {
The illusory manticores dissolve into pale mist as Peter loses consciousness. I bank hard toward the king, falling into formation beside Flower.

"Flower, on three!" I shout. "Combined focus!"

"Wait—what about the voice?" Flower yells over the roar of her flames. "It said to leave!"

"I didn't stare down the Magium twice to get chased off by ethereal mood swings," I say. "If the ether waited this long, it can wait sixty more seconds. The king is the last piece on the board. We end this now."

}
"A grave error," the king murmurs, his hands tracing a dense defensive shell.

"We'll find out," I say. "Flower, go!"

"Right!" Flower unleashes a continuous column of flame while I hammer his perimeter with rapid lightning strikes.

As we pour mana into his guard, my perception splits. The perspective no longer flip-flops between planes; I register both worlds simultaneously. The only other time my senses fractured like this was under the Magium's erasure field in the seredium tower.

My primary focus rests here in the white radiance, but I feel the cold mud beneath my earthen cheek, the driving rain plastering hair across my face. My physical body answers my intent like a marionette tugged by distant cords.

Flower described her own earthen frame the exact same way. This is how she lives every waking second.

Footsteps splash through the puddle on the physical street. The king stands over my prone earthen form, raising an open palm.

"Your fortune runs dry," the king says, and crushing pressure bears down on my back.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch09b-Floating, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Floating)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Floating
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch9_targets,1) if (v_b3_ch9_backup == 0 && v_b3_ch9_premonition == 1 && v_toughness >= 4)
