#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 1) {
Before the downward force can crush my ribs, the king grimaces, stumbling back as the pressure lifts. Out in the ether, the Overseer breaks free of the containment box, pouring heavy fire into the king's rear flank while his dual-plane focus splinters.

I press the advantage where our strength lies. Flower, the drone, and I converge on the king in the ether, pounding his flickering barrier from three vectors until the aura shell shatters into blinding shards.

One final lightning bolt tears through his guard. The king collapses into the white glow, his earthen counterpart dropping face-first into the street below.

Peter and the king float motionless in the radiance.

A cold calculus settles in. If I end them here, the physical plane holds zero evidence. The rebel remnants will assume the Overseer's soul displacement destroyed them. Two lethal threats eliminated with zero political blowback.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0 && v_toughness < 4) {
The invisible mass slams downward, pinning my chest flat into the mud. I strain against the crushing weight, but an invisible hammer crashes into the base of my skull.

The strike blows past my tolerances, blacking out my awareness across both planes at once.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0 && v_toughness >= 4) {
The invisible mass slams downward, pinning my chest flat into the mud. I strain against the crushing weight, but an invisible hammer crashes into the base of my skull.

Bone aches, but the maxed toughness stat absorbs the impact before my vision can fade. The king cocks his wrist for a finishing strike—

Twin whips of water lash from the dark, wrapping tightly around both his forearms and wrenching him backward through the rain.

The crushing force above my back lifts. I scramble out of the puddle, hauling my earthen body clear of his reach.

"Pardon the late arrival," Illuna's voice calls over the storm, her hands locked on the water whips. "I did not anticipate your dual-plane emergence."

"We're still fighting him in the ether," I call back. "Can you pin him while we finish it upstairs?"

"No," Illuna says as an explosive burst of aura shatters her whips into spray. "But I can keep him occupied."

She leaps back, flinging two thick water serpents into the mud. The constructs hiss forward, coiling around the king's legs; when he blasts them apart with his aura, the droplets reassemble instantly, lunging for his throat anew.

Divided between two planes, the king's ethereal barriers buckle under the combined onslaught of my lightning and Flower's fire. The shell fractures. One final electric arc snaps into his chest, dropping him into unconsciousness across both realms.

Peter and the king float motionless in the radiance.

A cold calculus settles in. If I end them here, the physical plane holds zero evidence. The rebel remnants will assume the Overseer's soul displacement destroyed them. Two lethal threats eliminated with zero political blowback.

}
