}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch09b-Elephant, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Elephant)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Elephant
TEXT:

A flash of white light—harsher, denser than the background glow of the ether—engulfs us. When the jump clears, the expanse looks unchanged, but the tension across my chest tightens violently.

"We're closer," I tell Flower. "The pull changed. It's not a small dog on a leash anymore—it feels like an elephant dragging me by the collar."

"An elephant..." Flower nods. "That puts your sanctuary right on our doorstep. Keep on that heading until—"

Her voice drowns beneath a deafening roar.

Millions of voices crash through my skull at once, accompanied by a blinding storm of flashing imagery—shapes, faces, fractured landscapes tearing past too fast to parse.

The chorus roars in unison, battering against my thoughts:

'Leave this place!'

'Get out!'

'You do not belong here.'

Clapping hands over my ears does nothing; the voices reverberate from inside my own brain. The flashing imagery breaks, and my awareness begins whipping between the driving rain of Ollendor and the glaring void of the ether.

The chorus falls dead silent.

A single voice speaks—the same voice that echoed across the duel:

'You were warned.'

My consciousness fractures, slamming back and forth between both planes a thousand times a second. A tearing sensation rips through the core of my soul, as if my spirit is being peeled away from my thoughts.

The cold returns, bitter and absolute. My ethereal limbs thin to faint outlines, dissolving into the surrounding radiance.

"—arry!" Flower's voice cuts through the static from miles away. "Barry, look at me! Look into my eyes! Barry!!!"

choice("Continue", B3-Ch09b-Visualize, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Visualize)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Visualize
TEXT:

I force my gaze onto Flower. She grips my shoulders, her red eyes burning like twin suns. Sheets of pure, harmless flame ripple across her skin, radiating heat that wraps around me without scorching.

"Barry, picture the inside of the cube!" Flower shouts. "Hold the image in your mind! Do you understand?"

"Yes..." The word barely carries past my lips.

I focus every shred of will on the memory of the sanctuary—the clean, featureless stone, the tight corners, the silence. I shut my eyes to lock the geometry in place.

"I have it," I whisper.

"Keep it clear!" Flower's voice cracks with panic. "Do not let it go!"

"I have it," I repeat into the dark. "What now?"

Behind my closed lids, the faint outline of my hands continues to thin toward total dissolution.

"—arry!" Flower's shouts break into fragmented bursts. "Listen—me! No time—no matter what—open your eyes! Do—hear me? Barry—losing you! Barry!!!"

A wash of teleportation light warms my eyelids.

The radiance of the ether cuts out completely. Pitch-black darkness presses against my eyelids.

The transition is over, but the weakness remains. Deafening silence settles around me.

choice("Open my eyes.", B3-Ch09b-Open, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Open, v_ac_b3_ch9_consolation = +1)
choice("Keep my eyes closed.", B3-Ch09b-Positive, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Positive)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Open
TEXT:

I force my eyes open.

No light answers. The void is absolute—an endless, suffocating expanse of nothingness.

"Flower?"

No sound leaves my throat. The darkness presses into my chest, heavy and cold. My strength drains into the emptiness, pulling my eyelids down one final time.

The dark swallows everything.

choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Positive
TEXT:

I keep my eyes locked shut. Flower's broken warning echoes through the dark:

'--no matter what-- open your eyes!'

The missing syllables are obvious: no matter what happens, do not open your eyes.

I hold the image of the cube steady in my thoughts—the six clean stone faces, the cold floor, the enclosed stillness. Nothing else matters. Just the cube.

Seconds bleed into minutes. Time loses its shape in the absolute void.

I'm still thinking. Still aware. Whatever Flower did, the dissolution stopped.

A bucket of freezing water crashes over my head.

I gasp, bolting upright as cold liquid drenches my collar. Solid cobblestone scrapes my palms. Driving rain hammers against my neck, lightning rumbles across the sky, and wind whips through the plaza.

"Are you going to open your eyes, or do I continue talking to a blind man?"

The voice is Flower's, but the tone is pure Illuna.

I open my eyes. Flower stands over me in the rain, twin flames flickering in her irises—ice-blue instead of crimson. Her physical form is solid flesh, soaked through by the storm.

The connection to the ether is severed cleanly.

"There was... an abyss," I tell Illuna, pushing myself up from the mud. "A suffocating void. Similar to the Magium's erasure space, but heavier. Oppressive. What did she do?"

"So she used the drop," Illuna mutters. "I suspected as much, but her thoughts were pure panic. I need to inform her that you survived before she works herself into a breakdown."

"She thought she killed me?"

Illuna raises two fingers, signaling for silence as she establishes her telepathic link to the ethereal plane. After several seconds, she lowers her hand.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch09b-Eyelids, v_current_scene = B3-Ch09b-Eyelids)


ID: B3-Ch09b-Eyelids
TEXT:

"Flower has settled," Illuna says. "As for your void—darkness is simply the absence of ether. The ambient light of that realm was hunting you, so Flower dropped you into the ethereal abyss where it could not reach. The only escape is to anchor yourself to a known location through sheer will. When your breathing stopped on this plane, I provided an external stimulus."

She holds out an open palm; a floating sphere of glacial water hovers above her fingers.

"Thank you," I say, wiping freezing water from my face. "Both of you. How did you even formulate that contingency?"

"Experience," Illuna replies flatly. "And necessity. It is not our first encounter with the abyss. Now excuse me—I must attend to Flower. Several matters in the ether require oversight."

"Is she safe out there?"

"For the moment," Illuna says. "Her altered state insulates her from the ether's hostility, though I cannot speak to its long-term stability. Wait here."

Her gaze turns glassy as her awareness shifts back to the ethereal plane, leaving Flower's physical frame standing slack in the rain.

I walk the perimeter of the plaza. The return to the material world feels jarring, almost artificial, as if waking from a vivid, hours-long dream. I had real magic in my hands out there. Real casting.

#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 0) {
Dozens of red-eyed drones descend through the storm clouds, mechanical prongs extending from their lower chassis to deploy stretchers. Working with rapid precision, the machines lift the unconscious rebel soldiers two by two, ferrying them into the sky toward the city center.

"The Overseer protocol assumes jurisdiction," a descending drone announces near my shoulder. "Thank you for your cooperation. The protocol extends a formal apology for the collateral soul displacement; the routine was experimental and exceeded perimeter boundaries. For alliance debriefings or municipal planning consultations, a green-eyed liaison awaits within the palace. Have a pleasant day."

"Where are you taking them?" I ask, but the drone lifts off into the rain without responding.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_backup == 1) {
